0 Fixture: a GRIP naming an item the figure is no longer holding.
0 Expected: problems. GRIP must fail closed when it excuses nothing.
0
0 GRIP tells the interpenetration pass to look away from one pair of
0 parts, which is exactly the kind of directive that turns into a licence
0 to hide a real collision once someone moves a part and forgets the line.
0 So GRIP is also an assertion: if the two named parts no longer share so
0 much as a bounding box, the claim fails instead of quietly doing
0 nothing. Here the camera has been slid 60 LDU clear of the hand.
0
0 The camera is decorative, so nothing else in the checker objects to it
0 floating -- the GRIP assertion is the only thing that catches this.
0
0 !LDRCHECK GROUND 8
0 !LDRCHECK FRONT +Z
0 !LDRCHECK GRIP 30089.dat 76382.dat
1 15 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 91405.dat
0 STEP
1 25 0 -40 0 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 73200b.dat
1 10 0 -72 0 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 76382.dat
1 14 0 -96 0 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 3626c.dat
0 STEP
1 0 83.69 -45.226 9.898 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 30089.dat
0 STEP
